==German==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|de|deyḱ}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|zēhe}}, from {{inh|de|goh|zēha}}, from an original {{m|goh|*tēha}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*taihwǭ||toe}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*deyḱ-||to point out}}. Compare {{cog|nl|teen}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈt͡seːə/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Zehe.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Zehen}}

# [[clove]] {{gloss|of garlic and similar plants}}
# {{lb|de|regional}} [[toe]]

====Usage notes====
''Zehe'' as meaning “toe” is universally understood, but rare in most regions. The form is common in [[Saxony]] (and bordering parts of East Central Germany) as well as parts of [[Austria]].<ref>http://www.atlas-alltagssprache.de/genus/</ref> The more widespread form is {{m|de|Zeh}} (of masculine gender).

